0,Yalarnnga language - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Yalarnnga_language,"Yalarnnga (also Jalarnnga, Jalanga, Yelina, Yellunga, Yellanga, Yalarrnnga, Yalanga or Yalluna[2]) is an extinct Australian Aboriginal language of the Pama-Nyungan language family, that may be related to the Kalkatungu language. [1][3] It was formerly spoken by the Yalarnnga people in areas near the Gulf of Carpentaria the towns of Dajarra and Cloncurry in far northwestern Queensland. [3][4 ...",Yalarnnga,Australian
1,Yalarnnga - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Yalarnnga,"Yalarnnga is an extinct Australian Aboriginal language, hypothesized to be one of the two Galgadungic languages of the Pama-Nyungan language family. [3] The last native speaker died in 1980.",Yalarnnga,Australian
